      "writtenOn": "2026-02-06T08:24:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We could do that. However, I think that approach introduces a third mutex to an already complex locking chain. It risks creating lock inversions. By the time `TryMapNow` is called, there are already 2 locks held:\n- First, command recording context\u0027s lock.\n- 2nd, the pending map list\u0027s lock in the queue. Acquired in `CheckScheduledBufferMappings`\n- Then another lock for mMapReadySerial (if we added here)\n\nFurthermore, since the mapping list is \"hot\"—iterating through 10-20 buffers per submission—repeatedly acquiring even uncontended locks forces unnecessary memory barriers. Given that we only need to protect against the occasional `Destroy` race, this adds significant overhead for a rare edge case.\n\nAlternatively, I have implemented a proper `Queue::CancelScheduledMap` method in the latest patchset. It should be self-contained in the Queue class now. PTAL.",
      "parentUuid": "82789c1a_7ac15550",
      "revId": "aebec50c77ce81b5479fbc5383e42960e11d7e9d",
